⭐ Interview Tip

The expected solutions are either the Two Stack approach or the Single Stack with Previous Minimum approach. In your solution, whenever a new minimum is pushed, the previous minimum is saved beneath it. When that minimum is popped, the saved value is restored instantly. This clever trick allows push, pop, top, and getMin all to run in O(1) while using only a single stack.
